   }
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "Heat engines need a hot **and** a cold reservoir.",
  "The waterwheel analogy gets the \"drop\" idea right, but heat is not conserved: \\(Q_1-Q_2=W\\).",
  "Clapeyron turned the cycle into the P–V loop; Kelvin and Clausius built the second law on it."
 ],
 "notes": [
